==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|hande mayden}}, {{m|enm|handmaiden}}, {{m|enm|hand mayden}}, {{m|enm|hand-mayden}}, {{m|enm|handmayden}}, {{m|enm|hondemaiden}}, {{m|enm|hond maydyn}}, {{m|enm|hoondmaydyn}}. {{surf|en|hand|maiden}}.

{{senseno|en|woman who supports transgender rights|uc=1}} is an allusion to Canadian poet {{w|Margaret Atwood}}'s novel ''{{w|The Handmaid's Tale}}'' (1985), in which "handmaids" are women who serve the male commanders in a patriarchal dystopia.

